/******************************************************************************************
        Item: Sweet Jesus it is a big head
        Description: Big Head

        Log:
           Please note any changes that have been made to the file in Updated. Then comment
           the code which you have changed/altered/commented out. Please, do not delete any
           code which was written.

           Created: September 26, 1997

           Updated:
           VOCK changes (Sacred Head talking head, art rendered from medicaledical's 3D model):
             The "Sacred Head" exchange runs in the dialogue window with the bhead talking head
             (HEAD_BHEAD, talking_heads.h). Using the head opens the dialogue at once: the wake-up
             lines (121-125, floats in RPU) are its first replies, and "[Step back.]" replaces the
             step back that never moved the player. The 12-hour skip happens between two dialogues,
             the head turns good at "VERY WELL!" (144), and repeat visits get a short dialogue that
             turns bad. Where the player has nothing to say, the option is an unspoken action (msg
             300-315). Wasteland background, night version while the head sleeps, and it sleeps
             while the map is dark (season lighting, map_daylight; RPU used day, 7-18). Low-IQ
             characters get the 1000+ lines at every player line, not only the first.
             SacredHead=0 under [Additions] in mods\vock-fo2.ini (VOCK_SACRED_HEAD) restores RPU's
             behaviour: no dialogue window, the exchange plays as floats (Node004-Node007), and the
             head sleeps by day (7-18). The ambient floats and the steal-and-die floats are the same
             either way.
             Fix, always on: Node008 counted with n7count, so "WHAT?! STEAL FROM ME, WILL YOU?!"
             (154) showed twice and "DIE!" (155) never showed. Now n8count.
******************************************************************************************/


/* Include Files */
#define SCRIPT_REALNAME "ecbhead"
#include "../headers/define.h"

#define NAME                    SCRIPT_ECBHEAD
#define CUR_COMP_SCRIPT         SCRIPT_ECBHEAD

#include "../headers/command.h"
#include "../headers/specenc.h"
#include "../headers/updatmap.h"   // VOCK: season sunrise/sunset, as the map lighting
#include "../headers/talking_heads.h"   // VOCK: HEAD_BHEAD

#define VOCK_SACRED_HEAD (get_ini_setting("mods\\vock-fo2.ini|Additions|SacredHead") != 0)  //VOCK: mods\vock-fo2.ini toggle; a missing file or key reads -1, so the talking head stays on

// VOCK: dialogue helpers
// Player line x, or its low-IQ variant x+1000 (both exist for every player line in ecbhead.msg).
// dude_is_stupid_talk counts Smooth Talker, as the engine's option IQ check does.
#define PlayerLine(x, node)     if (dude_is_stupid_talk) then NLowOption(x + 1000, node); else NOption(x, node, 004)
// Unspoken player action (msg 300+), shown at any IQ
#define Action(x, node)         NOption(x, node, 0)
#define GAction(x, node)        GOption(x, node, 0)
#define BAction(x, node)        BOption(x, node, 0)
// Daylight as the map lighting has it (updatmap.h Lighting, which rndbhead.ssl runs): from the season's
// morning hour to the end of its evening hour, dawn and dusk included. Winter 7-18, spring and fall 6-19,
// summer 5-20. The head sleeps and the dialogue uses the night background outside it.
#define in_light(m, e)          ((game_time_hour >= (m)) and (game_time_hour < ((e) + 100)))
#define night_bkg               (not(map_daylight))   // map_daylight is the procedure below

/* Standard Script Procedures */
procedure start;
procedure use_p_proc;
procedure look_at_p_proc;
procedure description_p_proc;
